---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const title = 'Battery Calculators & Tools';
const description = 'Interactive battery tools: runtime calculator, bank sizing calculator and charging time calculator — with the honest adjustments each estimate needs.';
const canonical = '/tools/';

const collectionJsonLd = {
  '@type': 'CollectionPage',
  '@id': `https://worldbatteryhub.com${canonical}#page`,
  name: title,
  url: `https://worldbatteryhub.com${canonical}`,
  inLanguage: 'en',
  about: 'Battery calculation tools',
  isPartOf: { '@id': 'https://worldbatteryhub.com/#website' },
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonical={canonical}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={[collectionJsonLd]}
  author="World Battery Hub"
  dateModified="2026-09-17"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="byline">Battery Tools · Last reviewed 2026-09-17</p>
      <h1>Battery Calculators &amp; Tools</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Three calculators and a finder that answer the four questions every battery decision starts with — and each one
        carries the honest adjustments that make the number worth trusting.
      </p>

      <div class="takeaways">
        <strong>The four questions:</strong> how long will it run, how big must it be, how long will it take
        to charge — and which group fits the vehicle or case in front of you.
      </div>

      <h2>Which tool answers which question?</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Question</th><th>Tool</th><th>What it adjusts for</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>How long will this battery run this load?</td><td><a href="/tools/runtime-calculator/">Runtime calculator</a></td><td>Usable depth of discharge, Peukert rate effect</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How much battery capacity do I need?</td><td><a href="/tools/sizing-calculator/">Bank sizing calculator</a></td><td>Depth of discharge, autonomy days, system voltage</td></tr>
          <tr><td>How long until the battery is charged?</td><td><a href="/tools/charging-time-calculator/">Charging time calculator</a></td><td>The absorption tail, charger sizing</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Which battery group fits this vehicle or case?</td><td><a href="/tools/battery-finder/">Battery finder</a></td><td>Group code, case size, voltage — with the CCA standard</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>The assumptions behind the tools</h2>
      <p>
        All three calculators assume the <strong>nameplate capacity at its rated rate</strong> (C20 for lead-acid)
        and <strong>room temperature</strong>. Three real-world conditions bend the results: heavy loads deliver
        less than the nameplate (the Peukert effect), cold reduces available capacity, and an aging battery
        delivers less than its label. Each calculator's page states where its estimate stops being reliable —
        the honesty is part of the tool.
      </p>

      <h2>The methods behind the tools</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/runtime-calculation/">How to calculate battery runtime</a> — the full method with
        worked examples</li>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/sizing-calculation/">How much battery capacity do I need?</a> — sizing in depth</li>
        <li><a href="/lead-acid/charging-time-calculation/">How long does it take to charge a battery?</a> — the
        charging-time method</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Read</h2>
      <div class="takeaways">
        <p>
          <strong>My read:</strong> The best calculator is the one that tells you when it is wrong — and the
          battery arithmetic is honest only when its three adjustments (depth, rate, temperature) are visible on
          the same screen as the answer.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Why:</strong> A tool that hides its assumptions produces confident errors; a tool that shows
          them produces decisions. These calculators exist to be the second kind — the number, the method, and
          the boundary, all on one page.</p>
        <p class="muted"><em>My editorial view, not a purchasing guarantee.</em></p>
      </div>

      <p class="muted">
        Related: <a href="/lead-acid/">lead-acid knowledge</a> ·
        <a href="/lithium/">lithium knowledge</a> ·
        <a href="https://testing.worldbatteryhub.com">testing methods</a> ·
        Last reviewed: 2026-09-17
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
